# hookwake drives the UserPromptSubmit hook against worlds it builds under mktemp. Every file below is COPIED
# into those worlds (a dist-layout copy and a consumer-layout copy), and run.sh prints HERMETIC-CONSUMED for each
# at the point it copies it.
# The subject: the hook, and the beat that writes the argv record the hook joins on (A0 runs a real beat).
!core/hooks/ai-dlc-hookwake.sh
!core/scripts/wait-for-deliverable.sh
# The start-time helper both of them source; A0cx proves the hook finds it in the consumer layout.
!core/scripts/wfd-start-of.sh
# P2 calls the guard's --hold-status beside the hook; the schema carries every harness literal P5 reads.
!core/hooks/ai-dlc-dispatch-guard.sh
!core/schemas/harness-origin.json
# --dispatch reads DISPATCH_ID_PREFIXES from this sibling of wfd; without it every J4 refuses (exit 64).
!core/scripts/validate-adversarial-convergence.sh
# P4 binds each blockable role to an existing team-roles/<role>.md.
core/team-roles/
